What else should you learn for a Data Analyst job?
Excel is important, but combining it with these skills will make you more job-ready:
SQL: SELECT, WHERE, GROUP BY, JOINs, subqueries and window functions.
Power BI: data modeling, DAX, reports and interactive dashboards.
Statistics: distributions, correlation, sampling and hypothesis testing.
Business intelligence: KPIs, trends, profitability and communicating insights.
Portfolio: practical projects using messy datasets and presenting actionable conclusions.
My recommendation: Prioritize data cleaning, formulas, XLOOKUP, SUMIFS, PivotTables, charts, dashboards and Power Query first. Learn VBA and advanced statistical techniques after you are confident with the core skills.
